# A ring (radii 5 and 2) cut through a 10-high block from its side, its outer circle tangent to
# the block's top and bottom: refused as ZeroThickness at the tangent lines, where Onshape builds a
# CADFS part (00850232) of this form. A ring of radius 4 builds. Whether a knife edge left by a
# tangent cut is to build is the owner's call; restated in round numbers.
sketch base(on: xy) {
  o = rect(corner: (0, 0), size: (30, 20))
}
block = extrude(base, 10)
sketch ring(on: block.side(base.o[3])) {
  a = circle((5, 5), 5)
  b = circle((5, 5), 2)
}
tube = cut(ring, upto(block.side(base.o[1])))
